    "The original loop achieved only about 2 GiB/s because each dot product had one loop-carried accumulator dependency.",
    "Row parallelism starts at 2,097,152 matrix elements; official router and MoE-down shapes remain serial while MoE gate-up crosses the measured threshold.",
    "Top-10 routed experts run in parallel, with each expert's two GEMVs kept serial to avoid nested Rayon dispatch.",
    "The independent shared expert overlaps the routed-expert group only when the same measured BF16 work gate is active.",
    "Router top-10 selection uses linear partition followed by sorting only the retained experts; score and index tie-break order is unchanged.",
    "The independent large BF16 GDN QKV and gate projections share one Rayon scheduling interval; small or non-BF16 projections keep their original order.",
    "QSA key, value, and indexer projections run as three outer tasks only when all three are BF16 checkpoints and their combined work crosses the same threshold.",
    "Generation prefill advances every prompt token through the canonical model state path but evaluates the untied LM head only for the final prompt row.",
    "AArch64 NEON F32 dot products and query-head parallelism accelerate sparse attention; contexts below the measured work threshold remain sequential.",
    "This Apple M1 host has no BF16 arithmetic extension; the NEON path widens BF16 bits to F32 and accumulates with FMA.",
    "The final path keeps checkpoint matrices in their mmap-backed BF16 layout and creates no F32 weight copy."
